# Licensing

*This repository is released under two licenses, split by what a file is rather
than by where it sits. The reasoning is in
[`docs/adr/2026-11-24-harness-hardware-is-cern-ohl-s-firmware-stays-apache.md`](./docs/adr/2026-11-24-harness-hardware-is-cern-ohl-s-firmware-stays-apache.md).
Full texts are in [`LICENSES/`](./LICENSES/) and are never edited.*

Copyright 2026 FortuneLabs.

| What | License | SPDX | Text |
|---|---|---|---|
| Hardware design: `harness/hardware/`, meaning the KiCad project, custom rules, worksheet, BOM, and fabrication outputs | CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2, Strongly Reciprocal | `CERN-OHL-S-2.0` | [`LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt`](./LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt) |
| Everything executable: `harness/firmware/`, `harness/scripts/`, `harness/tests/`, `harness/doctor.py`, `harness/hardware/check.py`, host tooling | Apache License 2.0 | `Apache-2.0` | [`LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`](./LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt) |
| Documentation: `docs/`, `contracts/`, `todos/`, `README` files | Apache-2.0, as above | `Apache-2.0` | |

**Not covered.** The calibration procedure and the Layer 4 test vectors are not
published. A license states terms for what is released and says nothing about
what is not.

**Source Location**, as CERN-OHL-S-2.0 §1.9 uses the term:
`https://github.com/fortunelabs-io/direct-semantic-comm`

